zellij-bin

zellij-bin provides prebuilt binaries of Zellij for x86_64 and
aarch64, a terminal workspace and multiplexer for managing multiple
shells and terminal applications within a single session.

Features include tabbed sessions, tiled, stacked, and floating panes,
layout configuration, session management, collaborative sharing, and a
plugin system based on WebAssembly.

# Supported architectures:

Prebuilt static binaries are provided for x86_64 and aarch64 (ARM64).
To build, the matching tarball (zellij-<arch>-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz)
must be present in the directory containing the SlackBuild, e.g.
zellij-aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz for ARM.

# Usage:

Start a new session: zellij

Attach to a session: zellij attach <session-name>

List sessions: zellij list-sessions

# SSH note:

Zellij stores its session sockets in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, falling back to
$TMPDIR (usually /tmp) when it is unset. On Slackware, elogind normally
sets XDG_RUNTIME_DIR for both local and SSH logins.

If you cannot see a session started locally when attaching over SSH,
make sure both use the same socket directory, for example:

  export XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/$(id -u)

If XDG_RUNTIME_DIR points somewhere you cannot read, set
ZELLIJ_SOCKET_DIR to a directory you own (use the same value for both
the session and the client).

Homepage: https://zellij.dev/
